/ActualText (Core CPI inflation to see little progress between now and late-springAs expected the biggest driver of the slowing was gasoline and other energy commodities that contributed 0.35pp less to the seasonally-adjusted headline CPI increase in October than in September. Core CPI inflation has been less than expected likely from tariff impacts that have been weaker than projected \(perhaps because of the tariff rebates\).)
